## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 13b64ad6e3d4841c4f7b49aef0858c196cb2b5e6

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I searched the history of `BulkLoader.java` for the introduction of `loadUserTypes` (`git log -S "loadUserTypes(keyspaceMetadata.getUserTypes()"`), since that's the method touched by the fix. It pointed to a single commit, `13b64ad6e` ("BulkLoader: Allow UDTs to be loaded"), which is also the direct parent of the fix commit `0ee0b9633` in this history.

**(2) Specific change:** Commit `13b64ad6e` introduced `loadUserTypes(Collection<UserType> udts, KSMetaData ks)`:

```java
private static void loadUserTypes(Collection<UserType> udts, KSMetaData ks) {
    LinkedList<UserType> notLoaded = new LinkedList<UserType>();
    for (UserType ut : udts) { ... }
    if (notLoaded.size() == udts.size()) {
        throw new RuntimeException("Unable to load user types " + notLoaded);
    }
    if (notLoaded.size() > 0) {
        loadUserTypes(notLoaded, ks);
    }
}
```

When `udts` is empty (a keyspace with no UDTs), the `for` loop does nothing, so `notLoaded.size() == udts.size()` becomes `0 == 0` → `true`, and the method unconditionally throws `RuntimeException("Unable to load user types []")`. There was no guard for the empty-input case, which is exactly the scenario the fix commit addresses by adding `if (udts.isEmpty()) { return; }` at the top of the method.

**(3) Evidence:** The fix commit's diff is a strict reversal/patch of the logic introduced in `13b64ad6e` — it adds the missing empty check and removes the now-redundant `notLoaded.size() > 0` guard before the recursive call (since returning early makes that check unnecessary in the base case). No other commit between `13b64ad6e` and `0ee0b9633` touches this method (verified via `git log -p` on the file), so the faulty logic was present unchanged from its introduction until the fix.

I'm confident in this attribution — the bug was present in the method from the moment it was created, with no intervening modification.

